// @@@ For any index that is greater than or equal to 0 and less than the size of the list, it holds true that for all subsequent indices i, the value at index i in the list is the same as the value at index i in the old list. This implies that if the value at the specified index is null in the new list, it will also be null in the old list. Otherwise, the value at the specified index in the new list is equal to the value at the same index in the old list.

